{"step_index":748,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T06:57:42Z","thinking":"Chrome's exclusive debugging session on port 9222 might be the root cause of new WebSocket connection failures. A separate browser instance launched via a framework could potentially bypass this restriction. However, a key concern is whether this separate instance will inherit the user's Google login cookies, which are essential for accessing the target URL.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"import asyncio\nfrom playwright.async_api import async_playwright\nimport json\n\nasync def scrape_colab():\n    url = \"https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1u6mCyiyeT45QW6O0L-95tJ-csN6VEC17#scrollTo=bBtUZIG4wjco\"\n    print(f\"Launching Playwright to load: {url}...\")\n\n    async with async_playwright() as p:\n        browser = await p.chromium.launch(headless=True)\n        context = await browser.new_context(\n            user_agent=\"Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36\"\n        )\n        page = await context.new_page()\n        \n        try:\n            await page.goto(url, wait_until=\"networkidle\", timeout=30000)\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(\"Page goto timeout or error, continuing to inspect DOM:\", e)\n\n        title = await page.title()\n        print(f\"Page Title: {title}\")\n        print(f\"Final URL: {page.url}\")\n\n        # Wait a bit for Colab JS to render notebook cells if public\n        await asyncio.sleep(5)\n\n        # Check if login page redirected\n        if \"accounts.google.com\" in page.url:\n            print(\"[!] Redirected to Google Login. The notebook is not publicly shared.\")\n            return\n\n        # Extract cells and outputs\n        cells_data = await page.evaluate(\"\"\"() => {\n            const results = [];\n            document.querySelectorAll('colab-cell').forEach((c, idx) => {\n                const id = c.id || c.getAttribute('id') || ('cell_' + idx);\n                const code = c.querySelector('.monaco-editor, .codecell-input, textarea, .text-cell')?.innerText || '';\n                const output = c.querySelector('.output, .output-area, [output-anchor]')?.innerText || '';\n                results.push({ idx, id, code: code.trim(), output: output.trim() });\n            });\n            return {\n                num_cells: results.length,\n                cells: results\n            };\n        }\"\"\")\n\n        print(f\"Found {cells_data.get('num_cells')} cells in Colab DOM.\")\n        with open(\"playwright_scraped_colab.json\", \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            json.dump(cells_data, f, indent=2)\n\n        for c in cells_data.get(\"cells\", []):\n            print(\"=\"*70)\n            print(f\"CELL [{c['idx']}] ID: {c['id']}\")\n            print(f\"CODE:\\n{c['code'][:250]}\")\n            print(f\"OUTPUT:\\n{c['output'][:500]}\")\n\n        await browser.close()\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    asyncio.run(scrape_colab())\n","Description":"Scrape Colab notebook using Playwright","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\k4ran\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\e2c1cf9f-2dff-4bf4-a974-ef410441acfa\\scratch\\scrape_colab_playwright.py","toolAction":"Writing Playwright scraping script","toolSummary":"Create scratch/scrape_colab_playwright.py"}}]}
